Package: miadi-restore
Version: 0.1.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: miadi-config (>= 0.2.1), miadi-tmux (>= 3.7c), miadi-tide (>= 0.1.28), miadi-terminal (>= 0.4.4), git
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: tmux sessions and their agents that come back after a reboot
 Installs what session restore needs and nothing else: miadi-config,
 the host's MIADI_* settings, miadi-tmux, one tmux (3.7c) in place of the
 distribution's, miadi-tide, the tide runtime whose daemon brings the
 agents back, miadi-terminal, whose `miadi-terminal enable restore` each
 user runs once, and git, which enable uses to fetch the tmux plugins.
 .
 A tmux server already running keeps running after the distribution's
 tmux is replaced, and a 3.7c client cannot attach to it
 (jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit#115).
